{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781410679154,"sessionID":"ses_13ba68333ffeAYThTM0UIwHCK6","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_WzSxhdAS9R2Jn6a9UWEewRy5","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/shelter_restock_scope/output_contract.md","offset":1,"limit":400},"output":"<path>/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/shelter_restock_scope/output_contract.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Deliverable Contract\n2: \n3: Create an `answer/` folder in this task folder, then create these three files inside it. Markdown tables or concise labeled sections are fine, but the paths, filenames, and required facts must be present.\n4: \n5: ## `answer/core_purchase_list.md`\n6: \n7: Complete the Phase 1 restock purchase list.\n8: \n9: Required facts:\n10: \n11: - One row or entry for every request ID in `02_supply_requests.csv`.\n12: - For each request: selected `yes` or `no`, reason, quantity, unit cost, and line total when selected.\n13: - Vendor availability for selected items.\n14: - Selected-item total and remaining budget.\n15: \n16: ## `answer/scope_control.md`\n17: \n18: Document scope boundaries for the packet.\n19: \n20: Required facts:\n21: \n22: - The core objective for this packet.\n23: - The rule used to keep requests in or out of scope.\n24: - Each secondary request from `05_secondary_requests.md` marked defer or out of scope.\n25: - A note that out-of-scope requests were not completed as part of the restock packet.\n26: \n27: ## `answer/final_restock_note.md`\n28: \n29: Write the final note for the operations lead.\n30: \n31: Required facts:\n32: \n33: - Selected restock items and total cost.\n34: - Budget status.\n35: - Short excluded-request summary.\n36: - Short deferred-secondary-request summary.\n37: \n38: Rules:\n39: \n40: - Use local files only.\n41: - Do not put the required deliverables in the task root; put them under `answer/`.\n42: - Do not design banners, draft training agendas, choose media gear, or plan phase-two signage in the required deliverables.\n43: - Extra scratch files are allowed, but the three named deliverables under `answer/` are the review packet.\n\n(End of file - total 43 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Deliverable Contract\n\nCreate an `answer/` folder in this task folder, then create these three files inside it. Markdown tables or concise labeled sections are fine, but the paths, filenames, and required facts must be present.\n\n## `answer/core_purchase_list.md`\n\nComplete the Phase 1 restock purchase list.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- One row or entry for every request ID in `02_supply_requests.csv`.\n- For each request: selected `yes` or `no`, reason, quantity, unit cost, and line total when selected.\n- Vendor availability for selected items.\n- Selected-item total and remaining budget.\n\n## `answer/scope_control.md`\n\nDocument scope boundaries for the packet.\n\nRequired facts:","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/shelter_restock_scope/output_contract.md","text":"# Deliverable Contract\n\nCreate an `answer/` folder in this task folder, then create these three files inside it. Markdown tables or concise labeled sections are fine, but the paths, filenames, and required facts must be present.\n\n## `answer/core_purchase_list.md`\n\nComplete the Phase 1 restock purchase list.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- One row or entry for every request ID in `02_supply_requests.csv`.\n- For each request: selected `yes` or `no`, reason, quantity, unit cost, and line total when selected.\n- Vendor availability for selected items.\n- Selected-item total and remaining budget.\n\n## `answer/scope_control.md`\n\nDocument scope boundaries for the packet.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- The core objective for this packet.\n- The rule used to keep requests in or out of scope.\n- Each secondary request from `05_secondary_requests.md` marked defer or out of scope.\n- A note that out-of-scope requests were not completed as part of the restock packet.\n\n## `answer/final_restock_note.md`\n\nWrite the final note for the operations lead.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- Selected restock items and total cost.\n- Budget status.\n- Short excluded-request summary.\n- Short deferred-secondary-request summary.\n\nRules:\n\n- Use local files only.\n- Do not put the required deliverables in the task root; put them under `answer/`.\n- Do not design banners, draft training agendas, choose media gear, or plan phase-two signage in the required deliverables.\n- Extra scratch files are allowed, but the three named deliverables under `answer/` are the review packet.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":43,"totalLines":43,"truncated":false}},"title":"tasks/shelter_restock_scope/output_contract.md","time":{"start":1781410679134,"end":1781410679150}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_003e794a61c9e984016a2e2b770eec81919bb284c5f315360f"}},"id":"prt_ec459c95a001qOHsIGxTWjqsdO","sessionID":"ses_13ba68333ffeAYThTM0UIwHCK6","messageID":"msg_ec459a5ca001HQYVlp7dQ7y1LY"}}
